  "goodToKnow": "Die Rute is a thin rod or switch: die Angelrute (fishing rod), die Wünschelrute (divining rod). In tradition, Knecht Ruprecht or Krampus, the companion of St Nicholas, carries a Rute for naughty children. Hunters also call a dog's or fox's tail die Rute. It was once a unit of length. Plural: die Ruten."
